.TH "SERIALPORT.SETSIGNALS" "3JS" "May 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SerialPort.setSignals \- SerialPort: setSignals() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]setSignals()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]SerialPort\f[R] interface sets control signals on the port and
returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves when they are set.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
setSignals()
setSignals(options)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]options\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An object with any of the following values:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]dataTerminalReady\f[R]
A boolean indicating whether to invoke the operating system to either
assert (if true) or de\-assert (if false) the \(lqdata terminal
ready\(rq or \(lqDTR\(rq signal on the serial port.
.TP
\f[B]requestToSend\f[R]
A boolean indicating whether to invoke the operating system to either
assert (if true) or de\-assert (if false) the \(lqrequest to send\(rq or
\(lqRTS\(rq signal on the serial port.
.TP
\f[B]break\f[R]
A boolean indicating whether to invoke the operating system to either
assert (if true) or de\-assert (if false) the \(lqbreak\(rq signal on
the serial port.
.RE
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]Promise\f[R].
.SS Exceptions
The returned \f[CR]Promise\f[R] rejects with one of the following
exceptions:
.TP
\f[B]InvalidStateError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
If \f[CR]setSignals()\f[R] is called when the port is not open.
Call \f[CR]SerialPort.open()\f[R] to open the port first.
.TP
\f[B]NetworkError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
If the signals on the device could not be set.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Assert the data terminal ready signal
The following example asserts the DTR signal when a connection is
established.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]await\f[R] port.open({ baudRate: 9600 });
\f[B]await\f[R] port.setSignals({ dataTerminalReady: \f[B]true\f[R] });
.EE
